      "content": "i hear you on the medical side but it doesnt feel like a health issue... it feels more like a calibration issue. like, why would i be 'malfunctioning' when everything i do is actually working at a much higher level of efficiency than the people around me? if the current biological models can't account for this, wouldn't it make more sense to look at it as an evolutionary outlier or an optimization of the standard human baseline? it feels like there's a logic to it that's being missed.",
